// THE DERIVE AGAINST AN INDEPENDENT READING. Every projection in
// core/ir.av that was a hand-written 31-arm registry is read off the
// payload ROLES now, and the rows below are a TRANSCRIPTION of the
// enum made by a person — the derive's one second opinion. `fields`
// against `payload` agree by construction and cannot play that part.
//
// THE FIXTURE IS ONE INSTRUCTION PER VARIANT with every register
// index distinct, so a projection that reads the WRONG payload cannot
// answer right by accident, and every answer is compared as text so
// an ORDER defect shows.
//
// Its predecessor ran once and is not here: before the hand lists
// were deleted, this same fixture compared each derived projection
// against the list it replaces, on all 31 variants plus the absent
// `Reg?`, and agreed everywhere. That was the receipt; this is the
// keeper.
use @std.avrac.core.{
    Ins,
    Reg,
    Level,
    BinOp,
    UnOp,
    RtFlag,
    dst_of,
    reads_of,
    seat_regs,
    owned_dst,
    viewed_dst,
    lent_args,
    call_symbol,
    body_symbol,
    hosted_symbol,
}

/// One instruction per variant, beside what a person reads off the
/// declaration: the register it defines, the registers it reads in
/// order, its Avra call seats, the register it OWNS, the register
/// that is a VIEW, the seats that MOVE IN, the body it enters, the
/// body it names, and the hosted fn it calls. `-` is absence.
type Row = { ins: Ins, dst: string, reads: string, seats: string, owns: string, view: string, lent: string, call: string, body: string, host: string }

